  :adr/body
  "# ADR-2607197700: PostgreSQL cross-platform matrix and scheduled soak

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

Pull requests and main updates require a non-fail-fast Linux x86_64 matrix for
PostgreSQL majors 14, 15 and 17 on JDK 21. A separate weekly macOS arm64 job
runs 1,000 operations from each of three contending guest workers through two
physical connections, with a 45 minute job deadline. The same interop program
accepts `KOTOTAMA_POOL_SOAK_OPS`; all network bytes remain host-bounded and
guest scratch is fixed and reused.

## Evidence

The configurable path completed 300 contended acquire/query/reset/release
operations against PostgreSQL 17.9 locally, in addition to the 90-operation
proof already run on PostgreSQL 14.19, 15.13 and 17.9. Terminal leases, waiters
and native handles are empty. CI owns the continuing Linux and 3,000-operation
freshness evidence.

This closes executable ownership of cross-platform and scheduled soak gates.
Their newest CI results remain required release evidence; this ADR does not
claim an unobserved remote run."}]
